# Root hints ship INSIDE the package (namespy/named.root) and are loaded through
# importlib.resources, so that file must stay tracked and must not be ignored --
# hatchling derives its default wheel/sdist excludes from this file, and an
# ignore rule here once meant a built wheel would have had no hints at all.
# Only a file dropped in the working tree for ad-hoc testing is disposable.
/named.root

# Traces the CLI writes with --trace; generated, never committed. Matches at
# any depth, which is how namespy/last_resolution.md got committed in the first
# place while being "ignored" -- it was tracked, so the rule never applied.
last_resolution.md

# Editor/agent scratch. Plans and workspace state are local working notes, not
# project history; committing them made diffs noisy and conflicted constantly.
.cursor/
.vscode/
.idea/

venv/
.venv/
debug-*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Build / packaging artifacts
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# Test, lint and type-check caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.mypy_cache/
.pyright_cache/
.hypothesis/

# Local-only caches and captures from manual experiments
*.sqlite
*.pcap
*.cap

# Where this session puts patches, junit dumps, candidate commit messages and
# one-off scripts. Untracked by design, and ignored rather than merely left
# alone: `ruff check .` honours this file, so an unignored scratch directory
# made a clean tree report findings that no CI job can ever see. Safe to ignore
# packaging-wise because the wheel lists its contents explicitly (pyproject
# `packages` / `artifacts`) rather than inheriting them from here.
.artifacts/

